{
  "configuration_id": "config_049",
  "reason": "The top 4 experiments (config_044, 018, 042, 040) all share scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + multiprofile + multimodal, and all four aggregation×fusion combinations within that family are now tested, with config_044 (transformer+weighted, 0.725) as the clear best. The single largest performance driver was the image encoder (resnet50→vit_l gave ~+0.08), followed by RNA encoder (scgpt→scvi_n200 gave ~+0.22). No untested configuration uses the full best component set, so the closest logical extension is config_049 (scvi_n200, resnet50, transformer, weighted), which isolates the image-encoder effect under the best aggregation/fusion. This confirms whether the ViT-L advantage is robust or whether resnet50 with transformer+weighted could close the gap, and rules out a cheaper near-equivalent. Expected cost is moderate (~7–8 GPU hours, comparable to config_001's 7.27 with resnet50+avgpool plus a small transformer overhead), which is acceptable given only one experiment remains after this one."
}

